\end{document}

This code uses the tikz library to create a simple chessboard layout with FEN symbols. The nodes are defined using the \node command, which takes two arguments: the coordinate (in terms of the grid) and the text content. The arrowheads are created using the \path command, specifying the direction of the arrowhead as north-east or south-west.

To add the FEN symbol, we use the \textcolor{red}{FEN} command, which sets the color of the FEN symbol to red. Finally, we connect the squares with arrows using the path command, specifying the coordinates of each square and the direction of the arrowhead.

